                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Pharmaceutical Analysis is a discipline that utilizes analytical and determination techniques to develop drug analysis methods, investigate the quality rules of pharmaceuticals, and conduct comprehensive analysis, detection, and control of drugs. Its main tasks include studying drug quality, formulating quality standards, and implementing analysis, detection, and control throughout the entire production process in accordance with Current Good Manufacturing Practice (CGMP), so as to ensure that the product quality meets the required standards.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
